{
  "_comment": [
    "DE4SDV INC-DRIVING-002, the driver-assistance bench. DRAFT, bench-only, not yet validated.",
    "The stack configuration of the SDV Core VM (/vendor/etc/someip/vsomeip_config.json), with the",
    "warning request's service added beside the two services the image already consumes. It offers",
    "no SOME/IP service: the SDV Core VM consumes service 0x4df1 (instance 0x0001, eventgroup 0x0001,",
    "event 0x8001, reliable TCP 30511) that someipd on the S-CORE host offers (interfaces/ICD.md).",
    "Each event's payload is the 8-byte struct of the ICD (big-endian, no length field); the broker",
    "translates it in REFLECTION mode into de4sdv.driving.v1.CollisionWarningRequest.",
    "__SCORE_SOMEIP_PEER__ is the S-CORE host's address on the VXLAN segment, 192.168.98.1 in the",
    "model; scripts/stage_sdv_core_interop.sh renders it from SCORE_SOMEIP_PEER, as the closed-loop",
    "driving bench's staging renders its 0x4df0 entry.",
    "0x4dee (reliable 30509) and 0x4df0 (reliable 30510) are the closed-loop driving bench's entries,",
    "copied unchanged from implementation/closed-loop-driving-bench/ivi-observer/interop/",
    "vsomeip_config.json: this file replaces the staged one, so dropping either would silently",
    "unconfigure it. The render refuses a result without both, and refuses to change either entry",
    "of the tree's current file. 0x4df1 is marked secure and accepted only from the peer, as 0x4df0",
    "is. The SD group stays 224.0.0.0, the S-CORE side's."
  ],
  "unicast": "192.168.98.3",
  "logging": {
    "level": "info",
    "console": "true",
    "dlt": "false"
  },
